  data: {
    LLM: "Free the Plait! The 13 cards in the Plait are your biggest obstacle. Don't use your stock cards or tableau moves if you could instead move a card from the Plait to a foundation. Every card you remove from the Plait increases your tactical options for the rest of the game.\n\nFoundation Focus: Since foundations can start on any rank (like an 8), the sequence is non-standard (8-9-10-J-Q-K-A-2-3-4-5-6-7). Pay close attention to the wrap-around. Don't trap an Ace in a tableau pile unless you have already cleared the Kings for all foundations.\n\nThe Alternating Trap: While you build down in alternating colors in the tableau, remember that you must eventually build UP in suit in the foundations. If you create a long Black-Red-Black sequence in the tableau, you might be 'Burying' a Diamond and a Heart that are needed for early foundation building. Use empty tableau columns to 'Break' and 'Sort' your suit sequences whenever possible.",
    Player: "Free the Plait! The 13 cards in the Plait are your biggest obstacle. Don't use your stock cards or tableau moves if you could instead move a card from the Plait to a foundation. Every card you remove from the Plait increases your tactical options for the rest of the game.\n\nFoundation Focus: Since foundations can start on any rank (like an 8), the sequence is non-standard (8-9-10-J-Q-K-A-2-3-4-5-6-7). Pay close attention to the wrap-around. Don't trap an Ace in a tableau pile unless you have already cleared the Kings for all foundations.\n\nThe Alternating Trap: While you build down in alternating colors in the tableau, remember that you must eventually build UP in suit in the foundations. If you create a long Black-Red-Black sequence in the tableau, you might be 'Burying' a Diamond and a Heart that are needed for early foundation building. Use empty tableau columns to 'Break' and 'Sort' your suit sequences whenever possible.",
